-- Tests of the teachers' instruments of the first corona lockdown — the
-- circular תש"פ/7 (l4/circulars/2019-20_tashaf_07.l4), which carries the
-- State teachers' special agreement of 1.4.2020, and the circular תש"פ/6
-- (l4/circulars/2019-20_tashaf_06.l4), which carries the colleges' special
-- agreement of 31.3.2020 — held against the public-sector agreement of
-- 18.3.2020 (MMS-600). They sit beside the circulars and not in them (the
-- client, 2026-10-22: "assertions about a file should sit next to it, not
-- be included in it").
--
-- The agreement of 18.3.2020 covers no teacher: it reaches an employee
-- represented by the New General Histadrut (its §2(א)), and the teaching
-- scale is represented by הסתדרות המורים, so §23 of the Collective
-- Agreements Law never weighs it against a teachers' agreement. It reached
-- the wider public sector through emergency regulations (outside the
-- corpus), which stand aside for "another agreement" approved by the wages
-- commissioner; תש"פ/7 says in terms that the agreement of 1.4.2020 is one,
-- for the State teachers it covers. So the teachers' arrangement is not
-- the round's, and says so: no vacation days are charged, the salary is
-- unchanged, and the price is teaching on the spring holidays and in an
-- extended school year. Day by day over the round's period the teacher
-- loses no pay and no leave day where the round's employee loses one for
-- every day charged: nothing is given less. (תש"פ/5 forbids putting the
-- owners' teachers on unpaid leave at all; it is a duty on the owners,
-- with nothing to compare.) The circular's reach past the agreement it
-- carries, to the owners' teachers, is its own finding,
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_07-b, and is not re-filed here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `2020-03-18_framework-agreement_public-sector_covid-furlough`
IMPORT `2019-20_tashaf_07`
IMPORT `2019-20_tashaf_06`

§ `בדיקות חוזרי תש"פ/6 ו־תש"פ/7 — מול ההסכם הקיבוצי מיום 18.3.2020 (יציאה לחופשה)`

§§ `מי שההסכם חל עליו`

-- The agreement of 18.3.2020 covers no State teacher, by its own §2 and by
-- the law; the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers him, and is "another agreement"
-- for him under the regulations, so the leave agreement does not apply to
-- him. The agreement of 31.3.2020 covers a college lecturer in the State's
-- service or a college that joined it.
`a State teacher under the agreement of 1.4.2020` MEANS
    `emergency employee` WITH
        `graded on the teaching-employee scale`       IS TRUE
        `employed in the state service`               IS TRUE
        `employed by an owning body`                  IS FALSE
        `stage`                                       IS `primary`
        `days set by the Director-General's circular` IS TRUE

`a State teacher's employment under the leave regulations` MEANS
    `employment under the leave regulations` WITH
        `bound by another collective agreement`                 IS `the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers` `a State teacher under the agreement of 1.4.2020`
        `that agreement signed before or during the regulations` IS TRUE
        `that agreement approved by the wages commissioner`     IS TRUE
        `that agreement takes no statutory right beyond the leave agreement` IS TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 18.3.2020 covers` `a teacher of the State in March 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2020 furlough employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in March 2020`)
#ASSERT `the agreement of 1.4.2020 covers` `a State teacher under the agreement of 1.4.2020`
#ASSERT `the agreement is an other agreement for` `a State teacher under the agreement of 1.4.2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the leave agreement applies` `a State teacher's employment under the leave regulations`
#ASSERT `the agreement covers` `a college lecturer in a joined college`

§§ `התקופות`

-- The teachers' period, 15.3.2020–18.4.2020 (35 days), holds the round's,
-- 19.3.2020–16.4.2020 (29 days), at both ends; the colleges' agreement runs
-- from the same 15.3.2020 to the start of the academic year תשפ"א.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL `the application period begins` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the 2020 furlough period begins`
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL `the application period ends` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the 2020 furlough period ends`
#ASSERT `days in the application period` EQUALS `the days of the 2020 furlough period` PLUS 6
#ASSERT `the agreement period begins` EQUALS `the application period begins`

§§ `יום אחר יום, 15.3.2020–18.4.2020`

`the days of the teachers' period` MEANS
    map (GIVEN k YIELD DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2020) PLUS k)) (range 0 34)

#ASSERT count `the days of the teachers' period` EQUALS 35

-- What a day of the round's period costs its regular employee: a day
-- charged to his leave, out of his balance or as an advance (§5(א)–(ב));
-- he is paid, his leave being paid leave. What it costs the State teacher:
-- nothing from his salary (תש"פ/7 §ד, the studies held) and nothing from
-- his leave — the circular charges none. A teacher with 9,000 a month and
-- an employee with the same salary and 10 days' balance: on each of the 29
-- days the employee may lose a leave day; the teacher's salary is 9,000
-- throughout and loses none.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD `the salary through the application period` TRUE 9000 EQUALS JUST 9000)
            `the days of the teachers' period`
`the round's leave days charged in all, with 10 days' balance` MEANS
    `furlough days out of his balance, of 18.3.2020` 10 `the days of the 2020 furlough period`
    PLUS `furlough days as an advance, of 18.3.2020` 10 `the days of the 2020 furlough period`

#ASSERT `the round's leave days charged in all, with 10 days' balance` EQUALS `the days of the 2020 furlough period`
#ASSERT count (filter `in the 2020 furlough period` `the days of the teachers' period`) EQUALS 29

-- The teacher's price, in place of the leave: teaching on four of the
-- spring holidays (three named for a mixed institution, which sets a
-- fourth), every one of them inside the round's period too.
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `a holiday day on which studies are held` `Jewish sector` d) `the days of the teachers' period`) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD (NOT `a holiday day on which studies are held` `Jewish sector` d) OR `in the 2020 furlough period` d)
            `the days of the teachers' period`

-- Sick pay: the round's regular employee has none for the period
-- (§5(ט)), save a note issued before 15.3.2020; the teachers' instruments
-- take none away, so their existing rules stand. Not less.
#ASSERT NOT `sick pay for a day of the period, of 18.3.2020` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 2020))

§§ `ההארכה ביולי–אוגוסט וחופשה ללא תשלום`

-- The round lets the employer call an employee who would be absent with
-- pay in July–August 2020 back to work then, the school year's extension
-- included, for no more days than he was on leave, in place of the days
-- charged (§5(ז)). The teachers work the extended school year in
-- proportion to the period they were not on unpaid leave (תש"פ/7 §ה), and
-- none of it is charged to their leave. Neither reaches one on unpaid leave
-- for the whole period (§5(ח) there; §ה here).
#ASSERT `days left charged after the call-back, of 18.3.2020` 20 20 20 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `§5 of 18.3.2020 applies to him for the time` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `extension days a teacher works` `days in the application period` 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `extension days a teacher works` 0 10 EQUALS 10

§§ `המכללות`

-- The colleges' lecturers keep the consideration in full for semester B
-- whatever was reported (תש"פ/6 §3), are paid nothing beyond it for the
-- duties put off, and charge no leave: their price is completing the
-- deferred duties by the start of תשפ"א.
#ASSERT `the consideration` 10000 0 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `extra pay for deferred duties` 2000 EQUALS 0
